cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.3+docmodel20-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * New Timeline panel (View > Show/Hide Timeline Panel, Shift+F9):
    - every edit is listed, newest on top, with the node, time and action;
      a node edited again appears again
    - clicking an entry opens its node and replays the change, switching
      between the state before and after it a few times
    - the changed area is highlighted while it replays, shaped like the
      change (text lines, the text inside a table cell, drawing strokes or
      a canvas), in a colour set in Preferences
    - the view stays still and centred on the change during the replay
    - selecting another node stops a running replay at once
    - autosave waits for a replay to finish, so the replayed state is
      never saved
  * Preferences > Timeline: enable (off by default), retention in days of
    use, number of replay cycles, highlight colour, clear the timeline
  * The timeline is stored next to the document (<document>.timeline, or
    timeline.db inside a multi-file folder); it is not kept for encrypted
    documents
  * Timeline: undo and redo steps are listed as "Undo: ..." and "Redo: ..."
    and replay correctly; replaying an older entry no longer shows text
    the node never had
  * Timeline: entries keep their place in the node when text before them
    is deleted, and the replay centres on the change as it was then
  * Fixed the OCR startup walk blocking node switches after opening a
    document
  * The OCR startup walk loads only the nodes with images not scanned yet
    (SQLite documents), instead of every node: much less memory used after
    opening a large document
  * Tests: GUI tests for replay of text, rich table cells, drawings, image
    edits, scrolling, highlight, node switching and autosave

